.TH LS 1
.SH NAME
ls \- list a directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ls
.RB [ \-l ]
.RI [ path ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ls
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
For each
.I path
(the current directory when there is none) that is a directory, it prints
the names of what the directory holds, one per line, without
.B .
and
.BR .. ;
a path that is not a directory is printed as it is.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-l
The long form: the type and permissions
.RB ( drwxr-xr-x ;
.B t
for the sticky bit), the number of links, the owner's and group's numbers,
the size in bytes, the time of the last change (UTC), the name, and for a
symbolic link where it points.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 if a path could not be read.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ls \-l /home
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cd (1),
.BR stat (1),
.BR tag (1),
.BR sh (1)
